1
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for the sun
sinking over the Naka River,

2
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:42,300
It landed on the head of
a carpenter who was jogging.

4
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,460
They laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if you lose your spirit,
Katsushika has plenty.

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:58,600
Even a yawn is no different.

7
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,540
The streets somehow feel so kind.

8
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:10,460
From the water tower with its pointed cap,

9
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:16,800
the sun sets down the back alleys.

10
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:25,240
Tomorrow will end this way too, won't it.

11
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:29,060
Even after losing,
happiness will come again.

12
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,760
I only realized it after losing it.

13
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,860
Because I'm such a fool.

14
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:41,060
Is it still too early for the Olympics?

15
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:48,140
Hey! You're going way too fast!

16
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:51,822
Hey, we'll eat ramen at Kogikubo and

17
00:01:51,872 --> 00:01:54,860
you say crazy things like
"round trip in one hour," you know.

18
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:56,200
Well, it can't be helped, okay?

19
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:59,580
I just suddenly felt like having Kogikubo ramen,
that's all.

20
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:07,060
Tch, there's always traffic jams here.

21
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:10,920
You're not coming here for ramen all the time,
are you?

22
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,780
Not like Yotsu-no-danna, you know.

23
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:17,100
N-no way!

24
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:17,680
What?

25
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:21,520
Damn, I can't tell like this.

26
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:23,900
Senpai, what's wrong?

27
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:27,400
If we keep this up,
the Chief's going to chew us out again.

28
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,800
Higurashi was over there.

29
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:31,560
Higurashi?

30
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:35,540
You mean that Olympic guy, Higurashi?

31
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:36,240
Yeah.

32
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:40,820
If you're Kochikame fans,
you probably already know,

33
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:44,420
but let me explain
Higurashi for newer viewers.

34
00:02:44,420 --> 00:02:46,540
His full name is Neruo Higurashi.

35
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:51,920
He's an officer at the same
Kameari Park police box.

36
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:54,222
He has psychic powers
like astral projection,

37
00:02:54,272 --> 00:02:56,860
telekinesis, and psychic photography.

38
00:02:56,860 --> 00:03:00,860
He's an amazing guy who solves
one unsolved case after another,

39
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:05,020
but using his powers seems to
drain his stamina enormously,

40
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:08,054
so he sleeps for 20 hours,

41
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:10,160
then 50 hours, and it keeps growing,

42
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:14,020
until he only wakes up
once every four years.

43
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:19,620
Since that coincides with the Olympics,
people call him the Olympic Man.

44
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:20,280
That's all.

45
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:23,980
Higurashi was walking around?

46
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:27,980
But Higurashi should have
been sleeping for four years.

47
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:33,200
Wasn't he woken during the Atlanta Olympics year?
So the next time he wakes up should be 2000, right?

48
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:35,580
Isn't it just a case of
looking like someone else?

49
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:36,580
No, it isn't!

50
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:40,720
I doubted my eyes for a moment too,
but there's no mistake.

51
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:43,760
He was wearing a business suit,
but it was definitely Higurashi.

52
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:46,780
Higurashi would never wear a suit!

53
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:49,360
And he was walking around Shinjuku, no less.

54
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:55,400
But if you wake Higurashi in any year other than an Olympic year,
he gets incredibly grumpy and goes on a rampage, right?

55
00:03:55,880 --> 00:04:00,580
That's right. Once he was woken between
the Seoul and Barcelona Olympics, and...

56
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:03,560
He's more terrifying than Daimajin.

57
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:07,100
He can blow up a building
or two without any trouble.

58
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:12,620
So far no damage reports from his psychic powers have been filed,
but if that happened, it would be a disaster.

59
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,340
Go check Higurashi's room.

60
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,720
Senpai, all we're doing is
checking whether he's asleep or not.

61
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:28,060
There's no need to
dress up this elaborately.

62
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,440
You've never woken him up,
so you probably don't know, but

63
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:35,580
Higurashi's room is more
dangerous than the Amazon jungle.

64
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:39,560
When we went to wake him two and a half years ago,
it was incredible, wasn't it?

65
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:42,160
If I remember right,
it was the room at the very back.

66
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:45,780
It's... it's too clean!

67
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:47,600
No way, that's impossible.

68
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,080
So he's awake after all, isn't he?

69
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:52,680
I hear singing coming from inside.

70
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:53,360
W-what?

71
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:57,220
That's the ending theme of Kochikame!

72
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:58,300
No way.

73
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:00,960
The ending theme when
he woke up last time was

74
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,720
Hoffdylan's "Smile."

75
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,760
He shouldn't know the current ending theme.

76
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:09,140
It's not locked.

77
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:09,800
What?

78
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,480
Nakagawa, open it.

79
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:15,660
We won't know unless we check inside.

80
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:16,860
Y-yes, sir.

81
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,740
He's, he's awake!

82
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:35,780
I knew it.

83
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:37,900
Hey, Higurashi!

84
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:42,580
Senpai Honda?

85
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:46,760
Isn't it? Do you know Mr. Honda?

86
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:52,320
He's my junior from later on.
Why are you living in this room?

87
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:57,720
Come on, Ryo-san.
I've been living here for four years.

88
00:05:57,720 --> 00:06:00,840
Isn't the room at the
very end Higurashi's room?

89
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:05,640
Higurashi? Right,
the room next door that was torn down...

90
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:09,220
Someone by that name?
What do you mean, torn down?

91
00:06:09,220 --> 00:06:10,820
I remember now.

92
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:15,880
Didn't they tear it down last summer,
saying they were widening the road beside it?

93
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,900
Come to think of it,
there was construction like that.

94
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:22,800
Didn't you say back then, senpai,
that it was in the way of the construction?

95
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:25,280
We dragged Higurashi-san out
while he was still sleeping.

96
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:26,520
I see.

97
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:29,700
I'd completely forgotten.

98
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:31,280
Come on, Ryo-chan.

99
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:35,000
So where did you move Higurashi-san,
the most important part?

100
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,580
Well, that's...

101
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:39,260
That's right!
We put him in the storage shed!

102
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,760
The storage shed is gone!

103
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:45,820
I-I'm sure it was right here...

104
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:48,940
Ryo-san, what are you doing?

105
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:53,140
Granny,
where did the storage shed that was here go?

106
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:56,802
That? It got old and the
door wouldn't open anymore, so

107
00:06:56,852 --> 00:06:58,680
we threw it out as bulky waste!

108
00:06:58,680 --> 00:06:59,820
What?!

109
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:02,000
What's wrong?

110
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,240
Higurashi was sleeping inside that thing!

111
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:05,760
No way!

112
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:08,120
So when did you throw out the bulky waste?

113
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:11,240
I think it was after the road-widening work,

114
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:13,520
last summer... Uh-oh.

115
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:17,240
Alright!
Rushing to the Yumenoshima waste facility!

116
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:25,655
It's the trash from last summer, right?

117
00:07:25,705 --> 00:07:27,960
Is it around that area, maybe?

118
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,120
Well, shall we head back?

119
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:34,040
Senpai.

120
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:34,840
Ryo-chan.

121
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:38,820
How are we supposed to dig through
a mountain of bulky trash like that?

122
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:40,260
Understood.

123
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:42,940
Let's have our company's
construction division handle it.

124
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:45,240
Looks like he's serious.

125
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,680
We're not finding it easily, are we.

126
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:57,880
If you buried a body here,
it'd be the perfect crime.

127
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:00,120
Don't say such tasteless things!

128
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,640
We found the storage shed!

129
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:07,060
That's it! No doubt about it!

130
00:08:16,540 --> 00:08:17,260
Found him!

131
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:20,640
Geez, you're really making
us go to all this trouble!

132
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:24,380
His heart's still beating.

133
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:27,840
Living cooped up in there for over half a year...
no wonder he's still alive.

134
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:32,180
Aaaaaah!

135
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:37,620
What are you doing?!
Get out of there, quick!

136
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:44,200
Damn! We woke him up!

137
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:53,620
W-what is this!

138
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:59,780
I won't forgive anyone who wakes me up!

139
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:07,360
Aaaaaah!

140
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:20,800
Uh-oh, when he's forced to wake up early, he gets in an awful mood and destroys everything!
Hey, stop it, Higurashi!

141
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:31,000
Haah.

142
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:31,320
Haah.

143
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:31,380
Haah.

144
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:31,880
Haah.

145
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:32,220
Haah.

146
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:32,280
Haah.

147
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:32,480
Haah.

148
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:32,520
Haah.

149
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:33,380
Haah.

150
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:33,720
Haah.

151
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:34,940
Haah.

152
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,200
Haa...

153
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:51,160
Haa...

154
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:57,800
Alright, it worked.

155
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,380
Reiko, good job.

156
00:10:00,380 --> 00:10:03,560
Nakagawa, Honda,
carry him to the police box for now.

157
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:04,080
Yes.

158
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:08,000
His psychic power...

159
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:11,920
Apparently someone's going to go on a rampage
at the Yumenoshima garbage disposal plant.

160
00:10:11,920 --> 00:10:14,940
That's you, you goddamn idiot.

161
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:20,780
I dozed off.

162
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:24,900
Anyway, let's head to the police box.

163
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:44,320
Where's the toothbrush?

164
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:48,000
I somehow got him to sleep.
He's a good sleeper, that one.

165
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:51,080
Senpai, what are we going to do now?

166
00:10:52,760 --> 00:11:01,460
Still, we can't just keep him lying here forever.
Higurashi has been sleeping in that storage shed all this time.

167
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:07,740
I wonder who Ryo-chan saw in Shinjuku. Maybe
it was a case of mistaken identity after all?

168
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:16,980
Fine, let's smack him awake and make him confirm it.
You idiot, we've been carefully keeping him asleep, and you want to wake him? Who does that?

169
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:18,980
What are we going to do if
he starts rampaging again?

170
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:19,780
R-right, I see.

171
00:11:20,420 --> 00:11:22,440
Then we'd better keep quiet,
or we're in trouble.

172
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:28,440
Yes, this is Kameari Park police box.

173
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:29,180
Yes.

174
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:31,160
Three Mori soba?

175
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:33,200
We're not a soba shop.

176
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:44,340
Well then, I've come to pick up the bowl.

177
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:45,920
Thanks for your hard work.

178
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:49,680
Whoa!

179
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:52,220
Idiot! Don't make such a loud noise!

180
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:53,120
S-sorry.

181
00:11:58,580 --> 00:11:59,840
Phew.

182
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:03,380
Ryo-chan, do something about it.

183
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:05,710
If Higurashi-san stays
in the back like this,

184
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:07,440
we won't be able to get
any work done in peace.

185
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:09,680
Easier said than done.

186
00:12:11,180 --> 00:12:12,080
Whoa!

187
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:13,240
What is it?

188
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:13,320
What?

189
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:17,760
Hey! Don't cause an accident right there!

190
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:19,820
What if Higurashi wakes up?!

191
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:21,120
Ugh.

192
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:26,120
Phew,

193
00:12:26,170 --> 00:12:31,020
That was close.

194
00:12:33,100 --> 00:12:35,780
Well, he doesn't wake up
even with that much noise.

195
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:37,680
I'm a little relieved.

196
00:12:44,420 --> 00:12:47,420
What?

197
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:50,940
You're the one who woke me up

198
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:52,640
Yeah!

199
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:55,260
He didn't even wake up to the
sound of a traffic accident!

200
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:56,380
How come?!

201
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:58,500
Waaaaaah!

202
00:12:58,900 --> 00:12:59,320
Senpai!

203
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:00,240
Yeah!

204
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,400
H-Higurashi-san...

205
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:07,380
Reiko! Quick, calm Higurashi down!

206
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:12,900
Higurashi-san, please, bottle up your anger!

207
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,060
This is a disaster.

208
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:27,840
Chief, we shouldn't let him sleep.

209
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:28,800
What?

210
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:32,400
If he wakes up every time,
he'll wreck the whole town.

211
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:34,780
In short,
we just need to keep him from sleeping.

212
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:36,880
But how?

213
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:39,500
I have a good idea.

214
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:45,360
Hey, Higurashi! Higurashi!

215
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:47,300
Going to wake him again?

216
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:49,800
No, no, calm down, Higurashi!

217
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,500
You're a grouch when you wake up.

218
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:53,860
I get irritated when I'm woken
up while I'm sleep-deprived.

219
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:55,798
Sleep-deprived? Yeah, right,

220
00:13:55,848 --> 00:13:58,720
you slept for a year and a half!

221
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:00,400
Did I really sleep that long?

222
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:03,180
It's Heisei 12 now, you know.

223
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:06,140
All of Japan is buzzing
about the Sydney Olympics.

224
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:08,920
Wait, wait, let me see that newspaper.

225
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:09,884
Uh-oh, uh-oh. This is bad.

226
00:14:09,934 --> 00:14:13,360
If I show it, they'll find out this fake
book was made from cut-up photocopies.

227
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:15,960
What do you think you're doing?

228
00:14:16,540 --> 00:14:20,380
I got totally crushed at the horse races.
It makes me sick. Just this junk.

229
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:26,960
Something seems fishy.

230
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:29,640
No, no, that's not true at all.

231
00:14:30,700 --> 00:14:33,380
Then what happened to
Nostradamus's great prophecy?

232
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:35,800
Nothing happened.

233
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:39,460
Then what about Namie Amuro,
the top idol from four years ago?

234
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:43,000
She married Sam of TRF and even has kids!

235
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,080
Then what happened to Hagakenji and Anna?

236
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:47,780
They finally broke up, damn it.

237
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:50,080
I see.

238
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:52,600
Looks like you've really
fallen behind the times.

239
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:55,320
Heh heh, just one more push!

240
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:58,320
Hey, you doing alright?

241
00:14:58,420 --> 00:15:01,240
Chief, the tea's ready in the back.

242
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:02,700
I see. Thanks.

243
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:05,940
Higurashi's awake? It's been four years!

244
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:09,400
Hold on, isn't everyone's
way of talking a bit strange?

245
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:11,220
That's not the case at all.

246
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:15,600
Nakagawa, would you have
Higurashi listen to the radio?

247
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:16,080
Yes.

248
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:19,340
Ryotsu, come to the back.
I need to talk to you.

249
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:21,940
Yes, yes.
Well then, Nakagawa, I'm counting on you.

250
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:22,500
Yes.

251
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:25,960
Higurashi always wakes up during the Olympics,
doesn't he?

252
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:29,640
Now that you mention it, that's true.
It's once every four years.

253
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:32,772
Good afternoon, everyone.

254
00:15:32,822 --> 00:15:37,440
Live from Sydney, we bring you the
final match of the football tournament.

255
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:41,261
Ichikawa intercepts the pass.
He breaks through down the sideline,

256
00:15:41,311 --> 00:15:44,580
passes to Ono.
Ono dribbles in on a one-man counterattack.

257
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:47,660
Japan's football team has made
the Olympics again after Atlanta.

258
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:50,920
Y-yes, and they've even reached the final.

259
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:54,960
Ono threads a killer pass.
Yanagisawa shoots, and it's in!

260
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:58,960
A goal's been scored,
but I can't get excited about it at all.

261
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:04,480
Japan! Jan-jan! Japan!
Jan-jan! Japan! Jan-jan!

262
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,780
Forget the soccer. I want to hear the judo.

263
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:08,820
Right. Yes.

264
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:15,380
Watching the Hinomaru,
Yahara-chan is crying.

265
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,580
Please listen to this cheering!

266
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,880
Tamura, did he win the gold medal?

267
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:23,040
Looks like the match is over.

268
00:16:23,300 --> 00:16:26,440
I wonder if the women's volleyball is on?
I really love volleyball.

269
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:30,840
Seriously? Seriously? I have no idea what's going on! Chief,
switch it!

270
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:32,960
Suddenly being told something like that...

271
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,980
Nakagawa, hurry up and switch it!

272
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:37,420
Chief, anything's fine, just hurry!

273
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:42,460
The ace of the women's volleyball team,
Kawanishi, this serve shines!

274
00:16:42,460 --> 00:16:45,340
They did it! The Oriental Witches,
Demon Coach Ōmatsu's...

275
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:48,060
That's strange, these are
members of the Tokyo Olympics team!

276
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:50,400
Nakagawa, break the radio!

277
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:51,440
Whoops, my hand slipped.

278
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:54,100
What a shame, we can't listen anymore.

279
00:16:54,100 --> 00:16:56,820
That's strange, I just heard a weird voice.

280
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,940
Hey, Higurashi, the Olympics were on, right?

281
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:02,080
It's Heisei 12, right?

282
00:17:02,380 --> 00:17:03,800
Somehow, that's hard to believe.

283
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:06,460
I'm going to go watch the
Olympics on TV for a bit.

284
00:17:06,460 --> 00:17:10,220
No way! Not allowed! You can't watch TV!

285
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:12,910
Hello, I'm from MHK,

286
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:16,060
here to collect the reception fee for April,
Heisei 11.

287
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:22,160
Heisei 11? Did you say Heisei 11?

288
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,100
Watch out!

289
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:36,560
How dare you deceive us!

290
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:38,280
Stop him, Neiko!

291
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:41,280
At that rate,
it's too dangerous to get close!

292
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:42,720
Neiko-kun!

293
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:46,180
Please, I'm begging you,
do something with your power.

294
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:47,680
Thank you in advance.

295
00:17:57,500 --> 00:17:58,060
Whoa!

296
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:02,360
Whoa!

297
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:05,060
Whoa!

298
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:08,180
Whoa!

299
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:09,500
Whoa!

300
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:09,940
Whoa!

301
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:10,520
Whoa!

302
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:11,460
Whoa!

303
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:15,600
Why is it always me who gets treated so badly,
damn it!

304
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:16,160
Why is it always me who gets treated so badly,
damn it!

305
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:18,960
If Reiko alone can't calm me down,
I'll summon Mars!

306
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:19,400
If Reiko alone can't calm me down,
I'll summon Mars!

307
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:20,040
Maria!

308
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:24,300
Ryo-sama!

309
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:28,880
Ryo-sama!

310
00:18:29,060 --> 00:18:30,200
Maria!

311
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:33,320
For Ryo-sama's sake,
I'll definitely stop him!

312
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:34,840
Yeah! Leave it to you!

313
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:41,500
Higurashi-san, please calm your anger.

314
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:49,900
This one might just work!

315
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:58,500
Isn't that a man?

316
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:04,220
There's no need for that!

317
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:12,551
By a mysterious psychic
who suddenly appeared,

318
00:19:12,601 --> 00:19:14,860
Tokyo has been thrown into utter chaos.

319
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:17,340
We have to stop him.

320
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:20,200
Something urgent came up. I'm heading out.

321
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,940
Section chief,
the meeting is about to start.

322
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:24,740
We'll join in real time over the internet.

323
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:25,340
Yes, sir!

324
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:26,960
We'll use the helicopter on the rooftop.

325
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:27,420
Yes!

326
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:40,920
Aaaaaah!

327
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:44,620
Haa.

328
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:46,300
Aaaaaah!

329
00:19:46,300 --> 00:19:53,600
He's like Godzilla, out of control!
You're the one who made him that way.
What is that helicopter?

330
00:19:57,840 --> 00:19:59,080
Aaaaaah!

331
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:01,140
You...

332
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:04,660
You're Higurashi, aren't you?

333
00:20:04,660 --> 00:20:05,860
What on earth is this?

334
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:09,500
Nice to meet you. I'm the twin younger brother
of Higurashi, the Sleeping King,

335
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:10,880
and my name is Okio.

336
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,880
I'm his younger brother,
you know, the hand-to-mouth type!

337
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:14,460
You never told me that!

338
00:20:14,460 --> 00:20:17,300
My brother doesn't talk
much about his private life.

339
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:20,300
Now that you mention it,
I've seen him in economics textbooks.

340
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:22,220
That famous corporate warrior.

341
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:22,900
You know him?

342
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:23,880
Yes.

343
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:27,980
For four years, he ran all around the world,
sleeping for about 40,000 hours in total?

344
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:39,660
An elite employee closing deals, truly a sleepless super corporate warrior.
I saw this man in Shinjuku. So this is your brother?
But he only wakes up once every four years.

345
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:45,420
Only I can stop my brother when he goes wild.
What? How?

346
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:47,580
The king has arrived!

347
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:52,980
Watch out!

348
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:07,060
The younger brother is a psychic too?!

349
00:21:07,520 --> 00:21:09,160
Their powers seem evenly matched.

350
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:13,260
The elder brother is still sleep-deprived,
so his power isn't at full strength.

351
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:15,880
Right now, I have the advantage.

352
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:17,120
You're reliable!

353
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,160
Yes, this is Igras.

354
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:23,020
Are you the director of Toyo Shojo?

355
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:24,120
Hello.

356
00:21:27,220 --> 00:21:28,820
Yes, it's about the
matter from the other day.

357
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:31,740
As for Toho, the answer of 20%

358
00:21:31,740 --> 00:21:34,100
Hey, don't be negotiating business!

359
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:35,740
Yes, understood.

360
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:37,380
Then, that's how it will be.

361
00:21:40,660 --> 00:21:41,780
The barrier...

362
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:49,300
Yes, I'll come by your place on business.

363
00:21:50,780 --> 00:21:52,560
Yes, then that's settled.

364
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:55,760
Negotiating business
while hovering in midair?

365
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,600
As expected of a corporate warrior.

366
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:00,360
I never thought he'd show up.

367
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,680
Good day!

368
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,700
Go back to the office and get to work!

369
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:08,140
Yeah!

370
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:09,880
Uni-san,
you're the one who should go back to sleep!

371
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:12,460
What a fierce sibling fight.

372
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,180
What a terrifying battle!

373
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:16,780
Somehow the damage has gotten even bigger.

374
00:22:24,020 --> 00:22:26,200
It's a missile attack from
the Self-Defense Forces!

375
00:22:26,460 --> 00:22:27,100
Don't go easy on him!

376
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,520
Go down already!

377
00:22:36,820 --> 00:22:38,320
Okio, don't get in the way!

378
00:22:38,700 --> 00:22:40,560
You're the one who should go back to sleep,
big brother!

379
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:43,760
Air Max Cell Expansion!

380
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:48,080
Yes!

381
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:56,220
What an incredible fight that was.

382
00:22:56,220 --> 00:22:58,460
That should put him back to sleep.

383
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:00,000
Mm...

384
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:04,220
Thanks to that, I'm wide awake now!

385
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:06,520
What? He's still full of energy?

386
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:08,500
It seems he's powered up even more.

387
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:10,540
Little brother, finish him off!

388
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:14,220
Hey, what's wrong?

389
00:23:14,220 --> 00:23:17,020
What's today's date?
What year and month is it?

390
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:20,580
Since he's been awake so long,
he seems to have lost track of the date.

391
00:23:21,100 --> 00:23:23,700
It's May 16th, Heisei 11.

392
00:23:24,220 --> 00:23:28,360
Sure enough, four years have
passed since he stayed awake.

393
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:31,060
He's entered his sleep cycle.

394
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:33,500
Looks like it! Hold on a second!

395
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:34,560
Hey, wake up!

396
00:23:34,620 --> 00:23:37,720
You're the only one who
can stop Higurashi's rampage!

397
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:44,480
Sleeping once every four years,
he's the complete opposite of his brother.

398
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:46,920
This is no time for you to be so carefree!

399
00:23:47,940 --> 00:23:51,340
How many people woke me up

400
00:23:52,820 --> 00:23:56,040
Yeah! I'm done with this,
I don't care anymore!

401
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:27,400
Calls come even in the dead of night,
and you wake up easily.

402
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:36,600
Even trivial talk warms my whole body.

403
00:24:36,820 --> 00:24:42,900
But I want to see my friends.

404
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:52,640
I surely want to be loved,
even if it annoys everyone a little.

405
00:24:53,460 --> 00:24:58,360
It feels like we're melting into each other.

406
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:07,880
I surely want to confide,
but somehow love alone is out of tune.

407
00:25:09,060 --> 00:25:15,860
Don't hide your bravado or anything else.

408
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:23,300
I was supposed to go to
Hokkaido for a marriage meeting,

409
00:25:23,300 --> 00:25:25,780
but by some twist of
fate I ended up in Kyushu.

410
00:25:25,780 --> 00:25:28,820
On the offshore island of Erabujima,
I find a fated encounter.

411
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:31,840
At last, after my long bachelor life,

412
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:33,900
it seems the time has
come to put a period on it.

413
00:25:34,240 --> 00:25:36,620
Next time: Burn, Love of Erabujima!

414
00:25:37,020 --> 00:25:37,640
See you then.

415
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:42,640
Thank you for watching.

